= Commonwealth Constitution Referendum

After months of campaigning and propaganda by both sides, the Commonwealth people have come to vote on the referendum for the revision of the Unity Constitution, which has taken the backseat in comparison to the devastating economic calamity. 

Passing the referendum would need to require the approval of more than 50% of those eligible to vote, rather than a majority of those that do vote [? if (gold_relation_9 >= 40 and gold_ideology_9 != "Right" and not lvp_formed) or ((lvp_ideology_9 != "Right" or lvp_relation_9 >= 40) and lvp_formed): This makes it impossible for the referendum to succeed, even with the recent economic calamity?][? if (gold_relation_9 < 40 and gold_ideology_9 != "Left" and not lvp_formed) or ((lvp_ideology_9 == "Right" and lvp_relation_9 < 40) and lvp_formed): This has made it difficult for the referendum to succeed, however with the support of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] and <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has made it a distant possibility, with the recent economic calamity?]. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #003755;">right</span> parties are also abstaining from supporting this referendum.

- @results: The nation votes...

