The referendum fails, with only around [+ weimar_ref_votes +]% of voters participating in it. It seems that the right is far more divided now than they were in supporting President DuFour four years ago. [? if weimar_ref_votes >= 40: However, the support for the referendum is higher than expected. ?][? if weimar_ref_votes < 30: The support for the referendum was lower than expected, this should weaken the right-wing parties. ?] The goal behind the referendum was not for it to succeed, but to rally the right-wing parties[? if (gold_relation_9 >= 40 and gold_ideology_9 != "Right" and not lvp_formed) or ((lvp_ideology_9 != "Right" or lvp_relation_9 >= 40) and lvp_formed):, which has failed since they've failed to recruit the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]?]?].
